fc1647dd6fd575a2d782204e94bf6ac171d0c830
exp_35 round 6a (iii-b): the supervisor's chunk transaction (plan r2 section 11 B2; r3 section 12 B2-B3; r4 section 13)

Supervisor.execute -- the baseline (time, his step, log identity) recorded at our first spawn, the GPU 1 reservation created O_EXCL with the lane, the chunk in_flight (atomic), the spawn: the runner on ONE cell or, for chunk 5, the launcher on the probe with the frozen argv. Supervisor.watch -- polls every <= 5 min, NEVER signals: a guard violation, a tuple / table failure or a NEW process on the lane (outside our runner's /proc subtree and the approved trainer) latches a stop after the running cell. verified -- the runner rc, then the receipt verified under the campaign's ONE digest (else the latch); gates -- E1 after chunks 1-2 (a mismatch or refusal: the hard stop), E2 after chunk 4 (PASS / FAIL recorded: the 45-degree source only; refused: the latch), chunk 5's finalization + PROBE_CONTRACT_BF with the section 13 NIT 2 ledger (probe rc, probe JSON / sidecar / final log sha256, the contract result), and the final guard on every chunk. reconcile -- an in-flight chunk at restart is adopted only if its receipt verifies (its gates then re-run), else the latch; a runner_verified chunk re-runs its gates first. run -- refuses a set latch or inconsistent reservations, walks the frozen order, releases the reservation at the end. Tests on the fake world: a clean campaign (33 chunks in order on GPU 1, reserved while each runs), the stops (guard, new process, his table job during a cell, rc, verification, E1, E2, finalization), E2 FAIL continuing, the hand-over (atomic, ALLOW_SHARED_GPU unset on GPU 0), a busy GPU 0 / another holder, PID reuse, the predictor, restarts, a rotated log, never a signal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--END--
f5a11e2ae8562c55b5acbca35c9ccd8b04ae8010
exp_35 Codex code C3b fixes (HIGH 1, NIT 1): the E2-FAIL artifact scan fails closed on I/O errors; a malformed guard anchor is REFUSED

HIGH 1: cell_artifacts treats only FileNotFoundError as absence; any other OSError while listing a parent of an E2-FAIL cell's artifacts (a permission error, a NAS I/O failure -- either could hide an artifact on an E2 PASS) raises RESULTS REFUSED, even with --partial. Tests: PermissionError and EIO for one relevant parent.
NIT 1: the guard checks the persisted anchor's exact schema and types (the keys anchor_of writes, non-negative ints, offset <= size, a 64-hex tail sha256) before anything is judged -- REFUSED (exit 3) instead of a KeyError; observe() and the CLI. Tests: eight malformed anchors through both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--END--
526308c82ab9926f01860793cb0e5745325f272f
exp_35 Codex code C3b fixes (BLOCKING 1, HIGH 2): the supervisor state carries the evidence of every claim; reservations are authenticated field by field

BLOCKING 1: state_reasons validates every top-level field exactly (schema, campaign, H35, cells / supervisor / approved-tuple sha256 -- load_state now takes the expected approved_sha256 --, the baseline {time, step, log {path, inode, size}}, the guard anchor's own schema, lane + reservation set together with one uuid, shared == GPU 1, an epoch >= 1 and the path's file name, a stop latch that is exactly a non-empty {reason, time}, events) and each chunk by its state: planned = the bare identity; in_flight = its lane, shared, started, log -- plus a recorded rc only under the stop latch; runner_verified / gates_verified = the rc 0 (None only when adopted at restart), ended, the receipt sha256 and the campaign digest (cells), and for gates_verified the passing gate result (E1 rc 0 equal; E2 PASS / FAIL consistent with its rc; chunk 5: the contract rc 0 and the probe JSON / sidecar / log sha256); a failed gate only under the latch; ONE campaign digest; a baseline exactly when a chunk has started; a started, unfinished campaign holds a reservation. 30 mutation tests (a fake gates_verified prefix, missing / failed rc, receipt, E1, E2, probe hashes, digests, another approved tuple, malformed baseline / anchor / lane / reservation / latch / events, extra keys) and five legal states (a crash mid-chunk, a latched failure, the completed campaign, a hand-over before the first spawn).
HIGH 2: read_reservation fails closed (unreadable / not a JSON object with a holder: ValueError); ours_reasons requires exactly the six fields, holder exp35, this H35, the branch, gpu_uuid == the file's own uuid, an int epoch >= 1 and a numeric time; reservation_reasons(dirpath, held, uuids, h35) refuses a malformed file or a stale exp_35 file; held_by_other never takes an unreadable file as free. The loop passes the new pins, records an adopted chunk's unknown rc as None and releases lane + reservation together at the end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--END--
0b9e1a3642a2994ce815160e7e444e075fd54843
exp_35 round 6a (iv): the supervisor's real world, the collector gates, the read-only dry run and the CLI (plan r2 section 11 R8; r4 section 13 NIT 3)

World: wall time and sleep; nvidia-smi --query-gpu=index,uuid / --query-compute-apps=pid,gpu_uuid (any failure or non-zero rc is a ValueError, so the loop latches); a chunk spawned in the repo with stdin closed and stdout + stderr in its log. CollectorGates: the gates through the collector's own CLIs at the pin, as CPU subprocesses -- verify (the receipt located by the collector's cell_paths, its campaign digest, then --verify-cell STEM --pin H35 --campaign-digest D), E1 (--exp35-ctl-check K), E2 (--exp35-e2), the probe (--finalize-bf-probe orbitrir_bf_cond_probe.json --probe-log LOG --campaign-digest D). dry_run: plans the 33 chunks with each chunk's state, gate, planning duration and exact argv on the current lane, then checks the live state READ-ONLY -- the identity tuple against nvidia-smi + /proc, the reservations, the guard over his log, the predictor for the next chunk, the latch -- and writes and spawns nothing (0 iff identity, reservations and guard hold). main: --dry-run, --external-shas (Yixun's queue script, evaluator and admission helper), the pins validated (exit 2), HEAD == H35 before a real run (exit 3), the reservation directory created only for a real run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--END--
